This site exists once per blog theme baudelaire ships, and the content is
identical in each. Whatever differs between them is the theme: the type, the
colours, the furniture around the words.

Every page here is a `.typ` file. The posts carry dates, tags and summaries, so
the listing, the term pages and the feeds all have something real to show, and
this page is #link("https://baudelaire.cstef.dev/features/build/typst-modules/")[the site's own catalogue]
rendered by the theme.

Have a look at #link("/posts/")[the posts], or at a
#link("/tags/typst/")[tag page], and then read
#link("https://baudelaire.cstef.dev/features/build/themes/")[how themes work].
